{
  "format": 1,
  "purpose": "R3_REALTIME_GCM_CONSUMER_FIXTURE_ONLY",
  "executable": false,
  "blockedBy": [
    "SOURCE_BINDINGS: the 30 requiredBindings are retained and verified (realtime-consumer-source03, 144 blobs); still unread: source.pendingBindings \u2014 the release migrate script, the RealtimeWeb.Socket wrapper and ErrorView (which settle whether a raised decrypt in socket connect / AuthTenant is the inferred HTTP 500), SynHandler (the connect_down path behind the bound join reason), the log filter, the RPC layer behind the bound join reason (rpc.ex, gen_rpc.ex), the rate limiters, Connect's RegisterProcess/ReconcileMigrations, realtime_web.ex, SignalHandler, TenantBroadcaster, nodes/region placement, the join payload, GetTenant, the replication poller, and the tenant_db_dump_15/17.sql that a fresh tenant loads before its migrations; crash-report shapes (Plug.Cowboy request crash with Server:/Request: lines; Connect GenServer crash with project/external_id metadata before the level) are inferred from Elixir/Plug.Cowboy, not captured; the two InitializingProjectConnection replies (realtime_channel.ex:227,230) can answer the same Connect crash and are accepted only with an attributed, untagged Connect crash entry",
    "POSTGRES_IMAGE: the supabase/postgres linux/amd64 manifest and config digests, its init behaviour (owner role, POSTGRES_PASSWORD, pg_hba, wal2json, anon/authenticated roles) and its effective config are not bound; pg_hba must require scram-sha-256 for the fixture subnet so the positive path proves db_password is used; supautils (reserved roles/memberships) may refuse the tenant migrations' GRANT supabase_realtime_admin TO postgres for a non-superuser tenant role \u2014 bind its settings, or make the disposable tenant roles SUPERUSER as upstream's supabase_admin is",
    "LIBRARIES: library tree hashes are computed on the execution checkout (--bind-libraries) and must be reviewed into this file",
    "BOOTSTRAP: the statements are an unreviewed draft. Per the bound tenant migrations each tenant DB needs before create: schema realtime (no migration creates it), roles anon/authenticated/service_role/postgres/dashboard_user/supabase_realtime_admin, a db_user with LOGIN REPLICATION, membership in supabase_realtime_admin WITH ADMIN OPTION and in authenticated, SET on parameter log_min_messages, wal_level=logical with wal2json, and at least 10 free connections; the metadata DB needs schema _realtime owned by its login role; the publication must contain gcm_fixture.events beforehand, and the slot must NOT be pre-created (Realtime makes a temporary wal2json slot)",
    "RUNTIME: the disposable linux/amd64 runner, its workflow (which must hand the runner an approval bound to that exact run \u2014 runBinding {repository, runId} \u2014 so a new dispatch cannot replay it), and the explicit digest-pinned image acquisition and import step are a later publication change; on that runner's Docker version the host must reach containers on an --internal network; tenant DB connections go through :inet6_tcp first (an IPv4 literal resolves IPv4-mapped), so the fixture network is dual-stack; the daemon must be Engine \u226527 with ip6tables enabled so the --internal network isolates IPv6 too, and both containers drop NET_RAW and refuse router advertisements",
    "CUSTODY: sealing the private evidence directory to the owner recipient is not wired into this runner"
  ],
